WEBVTT

00:49.049 --> 00:51.969
ALL CHARACTERS, INCIDENTS, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND BACKGROUND ARE FICTITIOUS

01:20.956 --> 01:22.332
Gu Seung-jun!

01:37.222 --> 01:39.308
Seung-jun, stay with me.

01:40.100 --> 01:42.602
Don't worry. I'm okay.

01:43.312 --> 01:44.313
No.

01:48.567 --> 01:49.443
Gu Seung-jun.

01:50.819 --> 01:52.195
Gu Seung-jun!

01:52.779 --> 01:54.823
AMBULANCE

02:06.418 --> 02:08.462
Hang up another IV fluid bag

02:08.545 --> 02:10.547
and check her vital signs again.

02:11.089 --> 02:12.174
Ms. Yoon.

02:12.257 --> 02:13.342
Ms. Yoon.

02:28.815 --> 02:30.567
Inject epinephrine through the IV line.

02:30.651 --> 02:31.610
Yes, Doctor.

02:47.959 --> 02:51.296
Ms. Yoon, can you hear me? Ms. Yoon.

02:51.380 --> 02:53.715
-Start CPR.
-Yes, Doctor.

02:53.799 --> 02:55.884
-Get the defibrillator ready.
-Got it.

02:56.093 --> 02:58.470
We'll begin defibrillation.
Charge to 150 joules.

02:59.930 --> 03:01.556
Charged.

03:01.640 --> 03:03.266
One, two, three.

03:04.518 --> 03:05.936
Charge to 200 joules.

03:06.019 --> 03:09.231
-Charged.
-One, two, three.

03:16.655 --> 03:18.073
Are you okay?

03:18.740 --> 03:20.033
Stay with me.

03:21.743 --> 03:23.036
Look at me.

03:23.120 --> 03:25.038
Look straight at me.

03:27.040 --> 03:28.375
You told me...

03:31.128 --> 03:33.088
that when you're doing better...

03:33.672 --> 03:35.590
Later on, if I visit you

03:37.092 --> 03:38.844
when I am doing better...

03:40.554 --> 03:43.181
And if

03:44.725 --> 03:45.809
you are

03:47.018 --> 03:48.562
still single...

03:52.065 --> 03:53.650
Then please give me...

03:55.318 --> 03:56.486
a chance.

03:59.156 --> 04:01.116
I was going to give you a chance.

04:03.410 --> 04:06.037
I was going to wait until you visit me.

04:07.831 --> 04:09.750
I was going to wait for you.

04:10.333 --> 04:11.585
I like you, Dan.

04:13.128 --> 04:14.588
Because I like you,

04:16.173 --> 04:18.091
I will keep in mind where I am going.

04:22.137 --> 04:23.346
I will live that way.

04:28.310 --> 04:29.895
I will do that from now on.

04:30.604 --> 04:31.855
I was happy.

04:36.526 --> 04:38.445
Hearing that...

04:41.782 --> 04:43.033
made me happy.

04:54.628 --> 04:56.338
Dan.

05:01.551 --> 05:02.719
That time,

05:04.721 --> 05:06.932
what were you referring to?

05:09.851 --> 05:11.019
Ramyeon?

05:13.230 --> 05:14.856
That man?

05:15.607 --> 05:16.650
Or...

05:18.860 --> 05:20.070
me?

05:21.530 --> 05:23.240
Why not?

05:25.450 --> 05:26.576
I like it.

05:30.247 --> 05:31.331
What?

05:31.873 --> 05:34.209
You like what? Ramyeon?

05:34.751 --> 05:37.462
Or did you mean that man?

05:38.338 --> 05:39.339
Or...

05:41.258 --> 05:42.133
me?

05:49.099 --> 05:50.225
You.

05:51.268 --> 05:52.352
It was you.

05:53.520 --> 05:55.230
It was you, Gu Seung-jun.

05:57.315 --> 05:59.109
I knew it.

06:17.043 --> 06:18.169
Gu Seung-jun.

06:19.337 --> 06:20.380
Gu Seung-jun.

06:22.007 --> 06:23.049
Seung-jun.

06:30.932 --> 06:32.183
Excuse me.

06:32.976 --> 06:35.395
I think he fainted. Please do something.

06:36.771 --> 06:39.691
Do something, please. Anything.

06:39.774 --> 06:40.859
I feel

06:41.526 --> 06:44.362
so bad for him.

06:44.904 --> 06:48.908
Please do something. Please!

06:52.412 --> 06:53.663
Wake up.

06:55.749 --> 06:57.083
Wake up.

06:58.293 --> 07:00.211
Please wake up, Seung-jun.

07:00.795 --> 07:01.921
Please.

07:02.589 --> 07:03.882
Seung-jun...

07:11.931 --> 07:13.350
It's back.

07:15.644 --> 07:17.729
-Give her the full amount of oxygen.
-Yes, Doctor.

07:34.788 --> 07:36.414
She's stable now.

07:38.333 --> 07:40.418
Let's wait and see how she recovers.

07:41.211 --> 07:42.212
All right, then.

07:53.682 --> 07:55.600
We heard she was in critical condition

07:56.893 --> 07:58.478
and thought we should be here.

07:58.561 --> 07:59.854
Thank you.

07:59.980 --> 08:02.565
I'm relieved. It sounds like
she passed the critical stage.

08:04.567 --> 08:05.610
Then,

08:06.403 --> 08:08.196
does he have to leave again?

08:08.989 --> 08:12.117
But her condition might worsen.

08:13.785 --> 08:16.705
And she might look for him
when she wakes up.

08:18.456 --> 08:21.251
Please see what you can do.

08:48.403 --> 08:51.031
It's nice to eat together like this.
It's been too long.

08:51.740 --> 08:53.616
Hey, don't laugh.

08:54.200 --> 08:55.577
Sorry?

08:55.660 --> 08:58.788
They might assume that we're some
kooky soldiers seduced by capitalism

08:58.872 --> 09:00.290
and think that we're easy.

09:01.041 --> 09:05.712
It's still not safe to assume
that their evil scheme has ended.

09:07.714 --> 09:08.840
What scheme?

09:09.799 --> 09:11.092
Think about it.

09:11.176 --> 09:15.013
I'm the most elite agent of the DPRK.

09:15.597 --> 09:17.182
They obviously wouldn't want to lose me,

09:17.265 --> 09:19.392
especially when I came down here
of my own accord.

09:19.642 --> 09:23.229
That's why they're feeding us so well.

09:25.523 --> 09:26.733
To tell you the truth,

09:28.318 --> 09:30.403
I already got an offer.

09:30.487 --> 09:31.321
"An offer"?

09:31.905 --> 09:33.615
In American Imperialists' terms,

09:34.616 --> 09:38.078
I guess I can say I got scouted?

09:38.661 --> 09:40.955
We can send you back
if you'd like to return,

09:41.998 --> 09:44.667
but what you wish to do
matters more to us.

09:45.668 --> 09:46.628
What?

09:49.506 --> 09:52.926
If you decide to stay,
we can help you get settled.

10:02.936 --> 10:05.271
They want me to stay.

10:07.482 --> 10:09.317
That's how capitalism works.

10:09.400 --> 10:10.819
Just like this saying,

10:12.195 --> 10:14.197
"Take what's useful
and ditch what's useless."

10:14.739 --> 10:17.742
They find my skills very useful,
so they're eager to keep me here.

10:19.744 --> 10:22.080
You always talk about
how much you hate capitalism,

10:22.330 --> 10:25.125
yet you seem to have already
acquainted yourself with the slangs here.

10:26.668 --> 10:28.169
-Well...
-But the thing is,

10:28.253 --> 10:33.091
he asked all of us
the exact same question.

10:33.967 --> 10:35.552
-All of you?
-That's right.

10:37.053 --> 10:38.513
You too, Eun Dong?

10:40.765 --> 10:42.976
Perhaps they did that
because they were afraid

10:43.935 --> 10:48.231
I'd think I'd get lonely and say no if
they asked me to stay here all by myself.

10:52.485 --> 10:54.904
Has anyone seen Captain Ri?

10:59.117 --> 11:00.952
Not even once.

11:01.911 --> 11:04.789
I tried asking the investigator,
but he won't tell me anything.

11:11.296 --> 11:13.548
A WEEK LATER

11:13.631 --> 11:17.844
I heard you suggested exchanging those
awaiting repatriation.

11:19.554 --> 11:20.889
We have a few from the South

11:21.472 --> 11:23.975
who are serving time in jail
for espionage charges anyway,

11:25.059 --> 11:27.020
so I'd say we and the South
have nothing to lose.

11:27.103 --> 11:28.438
No, it's different.

11:28.646 --> 11:32.025
The six soldiers who got arrested
in the South are still being investigated,

11:32.108 --> 11:35.945
whereas the nine South Koreans here
are already serving their sentences.

11:36.029 --> 11:37.155
The difference is huge.

11:38.781 --> 11:41.242
It's just us here, so let's be honest.

11:41.951 --> 11:43.328
The Military Department went ahead

11:43.411 --> 11:46.623
and prosecuted them without investigating
or putting them on trial.

11:46.998 --> 11:49.459
I bet some of them think it's unfair.

11:49.542 --> 11:51.044
Sir.

11:51.920 --> 11:55.131
You can never hide an awl in your pocket.

11:56.215 --> 11:59.385
You want to cover up
the fact that your son

11:59.469 --> 12:01.012
betrayed us for a woman.

12:01.095 --> 12:04.849
That is why you're trying to push ahead
with a deal that is so unfair for us.

12:06.392 --> 12:08.937
I'm sure they know
that it's a losing bargain for them.

12:09.020 --> 12:10.897
But they want them back no matter what?

12:12.023 --> 12:13.650
They obviously want
to settle this quickly.

12:13.775 --> 12:16.611
Yes, they want us to hand them over
as soon as possible.

12:16.694 --> 12:18.696
And they want to keep it confidential.

12:18.780 --> 12:20.823
They want the confidentiality term
to be five years.

12:20.907 --> 12:23.117
They're being sensitive about it
because one of them

12:23.201 --> 12:24.494
is a high-ranking officer's son.

12:24.577 --> 12:27.205
Are we sure that they never engaged
in espionage or any activities

12:27.288 --> 12:29.374
that serve the interest of the North
while being here?

12:29.457 --> 12:32.001
Yes. As you can see in the summary
of the investigation report

12:32.085 --> 12:36.130
and the statements signed by them,

12:36.214 --> 12:38.383
they didn't really do anything
except for the gunfight

12:38.466 --> 12:39.759
with Cho Cheol Gang.

12:40.343 --> 12:42.303
And how do they feel
about going back to the North?

12:42.387 --> 12:43.888
They all want to return.

12:44.597 --> 12:48.059
Then why don't we send them back
in secret as per the North's request?

12:48.142 --> 12:50.645
Going public with it
won't do us any good anyway.

12:50.728 --> 12:54.107
I agree. The conditions they suggested
are favorable to us.

12:54.190 --> 12:56.067
The Ministry of Unification
agrees as well,

12:56.150 --> 12:59.237
but we can't just yield to their request
without trying to strike a deal.

12:59.487 --> 13:04.075
How about we suggest a reunion
of the separated families as well?

13:04.200 --> 13:06.953
I don't think we have anything to lose.

13:07.704 --> 13:08.955
They'll try to strike a deal,

13:09.038 --> 13:11.708
to take advantage of this opportunity
and make the most of it.

13:11.791 --> 13:14.293
How will you take responsibility
for everything?

13:16.337 --> 13:17.839
I have a plan.

13:19.298 --> 13:22.135
-What's your plan?
-Pardon me?

13:27.015 --> 13:29.392
The South sent me these documents
on the evidence they found.

13:29.475 --> 13:31.519
Apparently, Cho Cheol Gang,
who defected to the South

13:31.602 --> 13:34.772
after committing countless crimes and even
killing someone while being transported,

13:35.565 --> 13:39.235
has been in contact with you
on a regular basis.

13:39.694 --> 13:41.279
Did you give him the orders?

13:44.782 --> 13:46.451
Of course not, sir.

13:49.162 --> 13:50.288
Right?

13:51.414 --> 13:54.250
You see, my son would never do
such a thing either.

13:54.333 --> 13:58.546
He'd never betray his country
because of a woman.

14:01.799 --> 14:04.969
Are you saying
we should cover up for each other?

14:05.053 --> 14:06.304
Is that what it sounded like?

14:09.474 --> 14:10.516
Fine.

14:11.017 --> 14:13.394
On one condition, though.

14:14.812 --> 14:17.273
The Military Department
will have full authority

14:17.356 --> 14:20.610
over the entire repatriation process,
including where we'll receive them.

14:20.693 --> 14:22.987
You wouldn't say no to that, right?

14:29.994 --> 14:31.162
Hello.

14:31.287 --> 14:32.955
-Nothing happened, right?
-Hello.

14:33.539 --> 14:34.582
Let's go in.

14:38.920 --> 14:39.962
Ms. Yoon.

14:41.297 --> 14:42.632
How are you feeling?

14:43.633 --> 14:46.844
-Good to see you.
-You look so weary.

14:47.011 --> 14:49.389
I'm okay now. Have a seat.

14:49.472 --> 14:50.681
Okay.

14:59.690 --> 15:00.566
When did you wake up?

15:01.150 --> 15:02.235
A few minutes ago.

15:04.737 --> 15:06.364
Would you please excuse us?

15:06.697 --> 15:08.658
I have to talk to Se-ri about something.

15:08.741 --> 15:09.951
-Sure.
-Sure.

15:13.162 --> 15:14.414
Se-ri.

15:15.415 --> 15:17.041
I just got a call.

15:20.545 --> 15:22.213
He'll be sent back to the North.

15:31.722 --> 15:32.849
When?

15:34.267 --> 15:35.476
When will he leave?

15:37.311 --> 15:38.229
Now.

15:45.403 --> 15:46.529
Now?

15:47.905 --> 15:50.575
Yes, he has to leave now.

15:54.454 --> 15:57.707
Seeing you now pains me more

15:58.791 --> 16:01.127
than the thought of
possibly ruining my entire life.

16:03.337 --> 16:04.797
That's great news.

16:07.675 --> 16:09.051
That's great.

16:11.220 --> 16:12.472
I suppose

16:13.347 --> 16:16.100
he didn't keep on lying.

16:16.601 --> 16:19.061
The investigation must've gone well.

16:19.770 --> 16:21.647
That's why he can return, right?

16:22.440 --> 16:24.233
I'm so relieved.

16:29.155 --> 16:31.491
Do you want to go see him?
Shall I take you to him?

16:39.916 --> 16:43.169
I've said goodbye to him
a number of times already.

16:44.003 --> 16:45.505
Too many times, in fact.

16:47.798 --> 16:49.800
I no longer have anything else
to say to him.

16:52.428 --> 16:54.472
And I don't want him
to see me like this...

16:55.973 --> 16:59.560
because it'll only make it
more difficult for him to leave.

17:01.646 --> 17:03.356
I don't even want him to know

17:04.232 --> 17:06.067
that I suffered.

17:14.033 --> 17:15.243
You think he didn't know?

17:18.538 --> 17:19.789
He...

17:21.249 --> 17:23.292
stayed by your side the whole time.

17:30.466 --> 17:33.135
EMERGENCY OPERATING ROOM

17:46.148 --> 17:47.817
Even during

17:48.568 --> 17:50.611
your long surgery...

18:27.189 --> 18:30.151
Why must we keep seeing her suffer?
It's so cruel.

18:30.234 --> 18:31.193
Come on. Let's go.

18:33.571 --> 18:36.657
Honey, I think I should stay here
for a little longer.

18:37.283 --> 18:38.159
What? Why?

18:38.242 --> 18:40.244
She could wake up anytime.

18:40.453 --> 18:42.913
I should stay by her side
because I'm her sister-in-law.

18:44.415 --> 18:46.375
-I'll get mad at you.
-Hold on.

18:46.459 --> 18:47.793
Come on. Let's go.

19:14.362 --> 19:16.822
Even while waiting for you
to regain your consciousness,

19:17.782 --> 19:22.703
he stayed by your side
without eating or sleeping for days.

19:30.711 --> 19:32.213
-Ms. Yoon.
-Mother!

19:32.296 --> 19:33.714
-Are you okay?
-She woke up.

19:33.798 --> 19:35.091
Mother, she woke up.

19:37.259 --> 19:39.553
Ms. Yoon.

19:40.137 --> 19:41.806
Ms. Yoon.

20:22.471 --> 20:25.558
WAITING ROOM

20:44.118 --> 20:45.911
He left the hospital after seeing you

20:46.829 --> 20:48.247
regain your consciousness.

20:58.716 --> 21:01.177
Even if you said goodbye to him
multiple times,

21:03.137 --> 21:04.847
you'll still miss him.

21:06.348 --> 21:07.558
You really won't see him?

21:09.268 --> 21:10.478
I want to see him.

21:12.229 --> 21:13.481
Take me there.

21:13.856 --> 21:14.940
Take me to him.

21:16.192 --> 21:17.943
I really want to see him.

21:36.128 --> 21:37.213
I have to say...

21:42.009 --> 21:43.636
Thank goodness

21:44.220 --> 21:45.387
that woman

21:46.263 --> 21:47.515
woke up.

21:51.727 --> 21:53.103
I know.

21:54.772 --> 21:55.815
We had no idea

21:56.690 --> 22:00.069
that Se-ri had collapsed
due to her illness.

22:03.239 --> 22:05.950
How could you guys have known that?

22:08.035 --> 22:09.745
After we leave,

22:10.329 --> 22:12.748
we won't be able to find out
how she's doing,

22:14.166 --> 22:18.212
so it's really good to hear
that she's regained her consciousness.

22:20.756 --> 22:22.383
She'll be okay now.

22:32.893 --> 22:34.270
Mr. Kim.

22:35.104 --> 22:38.649
Did you bring all these cars
because we're leaving?

22:38.816 --> 22:42.736
-That must've been a lot of work.
-Yes, it was a lot of work indeed.

22:46.490 --> 22:48.117
We'll never come back here, right?

22:48.200 --> 22:49.785
We shouldn't.

22:52.037 --> 22:54.206
It's raining cats and dogs.

22:56.000 --> 22:58.002
We won't need to come back here,

23:00.629 --> 23:02.881
but I'll probably think about this place
from time to time.

23:11.849 --> 23:13.601
Here we go. Hold tight.

23:40.502 --> 23:41.545
Hello?

23:44.381 --> 23:45.382
What?

23:48.302 --> 23:50.387
No, we do have some time, but...

23:57.269 --> 23:58.520
Where are you now?

24:08.489 --> 24:13.160
INTER-KOREAN TRANSIT OFFICE

24:34.348 --> 24:36.475
KAESONG

24:40.729 --> 24:43.357
Is that the Military Demarcation Line?

24:46.568 --> 24:47.653
Yes.

24:48.696 --> 24:49.947
I think so.

24:50.030 --> 24:54.868
So we'll be in the North
after we cross that line?

24:55.953 --> 24:56.995
That's right.

24:58.706 --> 25:00.999
All right. Let's get out now.

26:51.527 --> 26:54.363
We still have about five minutes.

26:54.446 --> 26:57.699
Why don't we have them cross the line
on the dot?

26:57.783 --> 27:00.327
We have a long way to go,
so why waste time?

27:01.328 --> 27:02.287
Let's do it now.

27:04.498 --> 27:05.499
Okay.

27:12.130 --> 27:13.215
We'll do that, then.

28:10.522 --> 28:12.983
No. What are they doing?

28:14.067 --> 28:15.110
Why...

28:17.029 --> 28:18.238
Jeong Hyeok!

28:21.575 --> 28:22.868
Don't run.

28:22.951 --> 28:24.578
Jeong Hyeok!

28:25.913 --> 28:28.248
You can't leave just like that.

28:28.332 --> 28:29.625
I can't let them take you

28:29.708 --> 28:31.668
-like that.
-Stop running!

28:31.752 --> 28:33.795
What do I do
if you just leave me like that?

28:34.671 --> 28:38.091
How would I live
after you leave like that?

28:38.175 --> 28:39.259
What should I do?

29:12.292 --> 29:14.711
PEACE

29:23.887 --> 29:25.889
You're not fully recovered yet.

29:25.973 --> 29:28.183
What if you collapse again?

29:28.684 --> 29:31.395
Can't you take better care of yourself?

29:32.104 --> 29:34.439
Why are they putting handcuffs on you?

29:35.232 --> 29:36.358
Are you getting arrested?

29:37.442 --> 29:40.529
No. I can't do that. I can't let you go.

29:40.612 --> 29:42.990
Don't leave. Can't you stay here?

29:44.616 --> 29:45.951
Don't worry.

29:47.619 --> 29:49.371
Do you not know me?

29:50.205 --> 29:51.415
Nothing will happen.

29:51.915 --> 29:54.126
But why are they dragging you over?

29:54.876 --> 29:56.753
What if something happens to you there?

29:57.587 --> 29:58.922
It's all because of me.

29:59.756 --> 30:01.508
It's all my fault.

30:04.094 --> 30:06.138
Nothing will happen.

30:08.640 --> 30:09.808
But even if

30:10.517 --> 30:12.436
something happens,

30:15.147 --> 30:16.898
it's not your fault.

30:18.025 --> 30:20.027
I have no regrets.

30:21.236 --> 30:23.947
You came into my life like a gift.

30:25.824 --> 30:27.326
I'm just grateful for that.

30:31.079 --> 30:32.122
Me too.

30:35.083 --> 30:37.419
Thank you, Jeong Hyeok.

30:40.672 --> 30:43.216
I broke your heart with my word
the other day.

30:44.259 --> 30:45.677
It broke my heart too.

30:47.888 --> 30:49.306
I'm so sorry.

30:50.098 --> 30:51.350
Please don't dwell on it.

30:51.933 --> 30:53.101
It's okay.

30:53.935 --> 30:56.813
I didn't mind it at all.

30:59.691 --> 31:01.234
Don't worry about it.

31:03.320 --> 31:04.321
So...

31:05.739 --> 31:07.366
Can't we see each other again?

31:07.949 --> 31:09.993
I will never get to see you again?

31:11.453 --> 31:12.579
Forever?

31:13.830 --> 31:14.790
What do I do?

31:15.957 --> 31:19.002
What should I do when I miss you so much?

31:28.512 --> 31:29.638
Just wait

31:32.307 --> 31:33.558
and pray desperately.

31:36.395 --> 31:39.564
You asked if you can meet
someone you miss that way.

31:42.484 --> 31:43.777
You can.

31:51.535 --> 31:52.786
I love you.

31:58.417 --> 31:59.751
I love you.

32:01.920 --> 32:03.088
I really do.

33:02.355 --> 33:03.732
Se-ri.

33:08.403 --> 33:09.779
Take cake.

33:10.906 --> 33:11.823
Se-ri.

33:12.908 --> 33:14.576
Stay healthy.

33:16.203 --> 33:17.120
Take care.

33:21.416 --> 33:22.834
Bye.

33:25.837 --> 33:27.464
Take care, guys.

33:31.092 --> 33:32.677
Don't get hurt.

33:54.574 --> 34:01.540
PEACE

34:18.181 --> 34:19.224
Really?

34:36.866 --> 34:39.703
-What are you doing?
-Are you going to pick Jeong Hyeok up?

34:41.913 --> 34:42.872
Make sure

34:43.415 --> 34:45.709
to bring my son home alive.

34:46.543 --> 34:47.627
Please.

34:47.711 --> 34:49.504
Do you think Jeong Hyeok is only your son?

34:50.922 --> 34:53.675
Whether something happens
to Jeong Hyeok or you,

34:54.259 --> 34:55.719
I will get there right away.

34:55.802 --> 34:57.637
Don't be weak

34:57.721 --> 35:00.265
worrying about how I hold up on my own.

35:03.018 --> 35:04.269
I'll see you later.

35:50.315 --> 35:52.275
Why are we getting off here?

35:52.359 --> 35:54.194
We were on our way to Pyongyang.

35:54.277 --> 35:58.031
You will be executed
after the court-martial after all.

35:58.114 --> 36:01.201
Wouldn't it be better to vanish here

36:01.284 --> 36:04.496
before causing your family trouble?

36:05.538 --> 36:08.458
Even if we end up dying,
we'd like to stand trial.

36:09.042 --> 36:10.543
And the comrades behind me

36:10.627 --> 36:13.588
just arrived late
after the Military World Games.

36:13.672 --> 36:14.881
They are not like me.

36:16.091 --> 36:17.550
I'm the one who committed a crime.

36:20.512 --> 36:22.055
It doesn't matter.

36:22.138 --> 36:26.101
We're just sending them with you,
so you won't be lonely on your way.

37:03.179 --> 37:05.682
Military Director. Didn't I tell you?

37:07.976 --> 37:10.770
You can't carry out an execution
without investigation and trial.

37:11.271 --> 37:13.523
It might cause innocent victims.

37:16.693 --> 37:20.238
But things are different

37:20.321 --> 37:22.699
when I witnessed someone
trying to kill my son.

37:28.580 --> 37:31.416
You can't be innocent.

37:31.499 --> 37:32.876
Damn.

37:59.611 --> 38:01.946
I'm sorry for making you worry.

38:02.781 --> 38:04.991
I'm just glad you're back.

38:07.452 --> 38:09.621
You came back alive.

38:10.163 --> 38:11.289
So it's fine.

38:15.210 --> 38:17.712
Is Yoon Se-ri all right?

38:19.839 --> 38:20.840
Yes.

38:33.520 --> 38:34.771
Are you crying?

38:59.796 --> 39:00.880
Mother.

39:14.686 --> 39:16.980
My dear son.

39:19.274 --> 39:20.316
Thank you.

39:20.900 --> 39:22.944
Thank you for coming back alive.

39:23.027 --> 39:25.613
I'm glad that you're alive.

39:30.952 --> 39:33.079
The roses of Sharon have blossomed.

39:36.332 --> 39:37.917
The roses of Sharon...

39:44.048 --> 39:46.634
The roses of Sharon have blossomed.

39:47.218 --> 39:48.344
U Pil.

39:49.137 --> 39:50.263
Dad!

39:51.848 --> 39:52.891
U Pil.

39:55.768 --> 39:56.936
Mom.

40:02.567 --> 40:03.401
Man Bok.

40:06.654 --> 40:09.115
I didn't hear a thing from you.

40:13.703 --> 40:15.079
I thought you were dead.

40:17.248 --> 40:19.500
Why did you not even give me a call?

40:23.046 --> 40:25.214
I'm so sorry.

40:27.759 --> 40:28.801
I'm sorry.

40:28.927 --> 40:30.637
Thank you for coming back alive.

40:32.347 --> 40:34.223
Thank you for staying alive.

40:45.068 --> 40:46.152
Failed again?

40:48.696 --> 40:50.573
What do we do?

40:51.908 --> 40:55.703
We have to talk to her.
She might get seriously ill.

41:13.137 --> 41:14.305
Please leave me alone.

41:14.889 --> 41:18.893
Dan, just tell us.

41:19.477 --> 41:23.523
What do you want your uncle
and me to do for you?

41:24.107 --> 41:25.358
Nothing.

41:26.734 --> 41:28.778
I don't want you to do anything.

41:32.323 --> 41:33.658
Please leave me alone.

41:35.410 --> 41:36.661
Why not?

41:44.252 --> 41:45.294
Look at us.

41:47.088 --> 41:48.381
We're here

41:49.090 --> 41:51.009
to cry with you.

41:52.176 --> 41:54.095
We can listen to you.

41:54.929 --> 41:58.224
And we can go through
all the hard times with you.

42:11.863 --> 42:13.072
Sure.

42:13.656 --> 42:17.785
And I can get you a guy
who's a lot better than him.

42:21.748 --> 42:23.082
Why?

42:23.166 --> 42:24.333
Damn it.

42:28.546 --> 42:29.630
Please get out.

42:34.886 --> 42:36.512
Why...

42:38.014 --> 42:40.391
Don't come near me.

42:40.475 --> 42:42.351
-What's wrong?
-Why did you...

42:46.022 --> 42:48.691
Why would you say that?

42:48.816 --> 42:50.318
Have you lost your mind?

42:50.902 --> 42:51.736
I was just...

42:53.446 --> 42:54.614
Dan.

42:55.198 --> 42:57.116
Why? Do you want to eat?

42:57.867 --> 42:59.744
-Mom.
-Yes.

42:59.827 --> 43:01.871
-Uncle.
-Yes.

43:02.789 --> 43:05.666
I want to get my revenge.

43:10.254 --> 43:12.465
We're experts in that field.

43:13.049 --> 43:14.300
Isn't that right?

43:14.634 --> 43:16.177
Sure. We are.

43:17.845 --> 43:20.014
I need you to find someone first.

43:30.024 --> 43:32.151
About Gu Seung-jun...

43:33.778 --> 43:35.071
I'm sorry about that.

43:39.784 --> 43:42.203
I heard some members of the gang

43:42.787 --> 43:44.997
who sent the guys that day
are still in this country.

43:46.582 --> 43:47.875
Right.

43:48.918 --> 43:52.130
Don't worry about the consequences,
and just tell me where they are.

43:52.547 --> 43:54.715
There's no way

43:55.758 --> 43:57.677
they will leave this country alive.

44:00.138 --> 44:01.889
And there must be people

44:02.598 --> 44:04.517
who financed the gang.

44:05.601 --> 44:06.769
Maybe...

44:06.853 --> 44:09.689
Her second brother was quite greedy.

44:10.565 --> 44:12.942
And the easiest thing to do is

44:13.776 --> 44:15.069
to tempt someone greedy.

44:15.153 --> 44:18.656
It's Yoon Se-ri's second brother,

44:20.533 --> 44:21.742
I guess.

44:27.081 --> 44:29.750
All right. Let me get this straight.

44:30.168 --> 44:32.545
I never asked them
to capture Gu Seung-jun.

44:32.628 --> 44:35.173
You did. Is that right?

44:35.756 --> 44:38.134
And Gu Seung-jun happened to die
in the process.

44:38.217 --> 44:40.970
That's what the people you hired did.

44:41.053 --> 44:44.390
It has nothing to do with me, right?

44:45.725 --> 44:47.226
Will you say something?

44:48.060 --> 44:49.812
When Manager Oh brought Cho Cheol Gang

44:49.896 --> 44:52.773
and said all the crap
like capturing or killing Se-ri,

44:52.857 --> 44:55.359
I got furious and stormed out of the room.

44:55.443 --> 44:58.821
It's you who ordered Cho Cheol Gang
to take Se-ri.

44:58.905 --> 44:59.864
You admit it, right?

45:10.458 --> 45:12.293
Yoon Se-hyeong, you know nothing.

45:14.795 --> 45:18.925
A recording without consent of the other
has no legal validity.

45:19.008 --> 45:22.511
Does it even matter?
I'm just stating the facts.

45:22.595 --> 45:24.430
Who would believe that?

45:24.764 --> 45:28.184
I did the whole thing for you,
Yoon Se-hyeong.

45:28.267 --> 45:31.771
For me? Don't give me that baloney.

45:31.854 --> 45:34.106
Think about the consequences
of what you've done for me.

45:34.190 --> 45:35.566
I'm now

45:36.400 --> 45:38.444
about to lose my position
as the president.

45:39.111 --> 45:43.407
If something goes wrong,
I might end up in jail because of you.

45:44.158 --> 45:45.409
Calm yourself down.

45:45.493 --> 45:47.745
It's North Korea
where Gu Seung-jun got killed.

45:48.496 --> 45:51.332
Why would they want to deal with a case
that happened in North Korea?

45:51.415 --> 45:54.001
I took care of things,
so the police won't find out

45:54.085 --> 45:56.963
the money we wired and call history.

45:57.254 --> 46:01.175
Even Cho Cheol Gang
who tried to kidnap Se-ri

46:01.384 --> 46:03.219
just died when we didn't do anything.

46:04.136 --> 46:06.305
We have nothing to worry about.

46:10.142 --> 46:11.644
Are you sure about that?

46:20.361 --> 46:21.862
When did you get out of the hospital?

46:22.446 --> 46:23.406
Today.

46:24.365 --> 46:25.908
I got here as soon as I left.

46:26.742 --> 46:27.952
Sit.

46:28.035 --> 46:30.204
This isn't your house.
Don't tell me what to do.

46:34.709 --> 46:36.168
When will you get questioned by NIS?

46:36.752 --> 46:37.837
I did it already.

46:39.755 --> 46:41.340
I think I'll be prosecuted.

46:42.216 --> 46:45.177
It's about the violation
of the National Security Act.

46:45.261 --> 46:46.887
You should get a good attorney.

46:47.054 --> 46:50.641
Don't worry. She will have my attorney.

46:51.225 --> 46:53.227
She might be accused
of misprision of felony.

46:53.310 --> 46:56.313
But there were extenuating circumstances,

46:56.522 --> 47:00.067
so she will be given
a suspended sentence or a fine.

47:00.818 --> 47:03.946
Still, it's not a minor crime.

47:04.280 --> 47:05.948
What if there's an article about her?

47:06.032 --> 47:09.410
Mind your own business. There will be
more than a probation for you two.

47:10.453 --> 47:13.080
-What?
-If you knew about the law that well,

47:13.622 --> 47:15.791
you should've been more cautious.

47:16.375 --> 47:20.004
Knowing someone is a criminal
or about to commit a crime,

47:20.588 --> 47:24.008
if you offer money
or other pecuniary advantage

47:24.258 --> 47:27.428
or provide a place
for communication, stakeout, or contact,

47:28.137 --> 47:30.723
you shall be sentenced to a penalty
of up to ten years in prison.

47:31.307 --> 47:33.059
What are you talking about?

47:33.601 --> 47:34.810
Come on out.

47:41.650 --> 47:44.028
I brought them from NIS.

47:44.236 --> 47:45.529
I'm sorry.

47:46.197 --> 47:48.032
There's a broker named Cheon

47:48.115 --> 47:50.576
who used to take care of Gu Seung-jun.

47:51.202 --> 47:52.870
He sent all the account details

47:52.953 --> 47:55.956
and phone call recordings

47:56.165 --> 47:58.584
to Ms. Yoon through China.

47:59.460 --> 48:04.632
I just did what these two told me to do.

48:04.715 --> 48:07.718
What are you talking about?
Who told you to do that, you idiot?

48:07.802 --> 48:12.014
Hey. How dare you
try to put the blame on us?

48:12.098 --> 48:14.391
I guess you two have a lot to talk about.

48:14.475 --> 48:17.645
This case is solicitation of murder,
solicitation of kidnap,

48:17.728 --> 48:18.938
and concealment of an offender.

48:19.021 --> 48:22.358
There are a lot of charges.

48:22.441 --> 48:25.611
The police and NIS will need
a joint investigation.

48:25.778 --> 48:27.154
Anyway,

48:29.323 --> 48:30.241
come with us.

48:32.451 --> 48:33.869
You said it will be okay.

48:34.078 --> 48:36.705
Go ahead and do something.

48:41.961 --> 48:42.795
Dad.

48:44.380 --> 48:47.133
Are you going to sit back
and watch me get arrested?

48:47.216 --> 48:50.594
You should think
about the image of our company.

48:50.678 --> 48:51.720
Shut your mouth.

48:52.304 --> 48:55.015
So you are a businessman.

48:55.850 --> 48:56.934
Do you still not get it?

48:57.017 --> 48:59.520
That I'm cutting you off?

49:00.187 --> 49:04.275
I'm cutting out the rotten part
before it gets serious.

49:40.477 --> 49:43.022
HOW TO MAKE SCORCHED RICE
HOW TO COOK NOODLES

51:17.241 --> 51:18.784
Are you still up?

51:20.577 --> 51:24.415
If you're reading my message now,
it means you're still awake.

51:26.292 --> 51:29.128
Jeong Hyeok, how...

51:39.138 --> 51:40.306
Click Message.

51:41.473 --> 51:44.393
Pick a date and time you want.

51:44.685 --> 51:45.811
Done.

51:48.981 --> 51:50.149
Write a message.

51:51.358 --> 51:52.693
Give it a try.

52:05.247 --> 52:08.042
I still worry a lot about you.

52:08.876 --> 52:11.462
And I have a lot of things left
to tell you.

52:12.588 --> 52:15.632
So I'm sending these messages
to tell you all of them.

52:17.968 --> 52:22.014
What I want to tell you the most
is on your bookshelf.

52:23.891 --> 52:28.354
I LOVE YOU, YOON SE-RI

52:28.437 --> 52:31.857
It's my reply to the message
you sent me before.

52:35.778 --> 52:37.529
I LOVE YOU, YOON SE-RI

52:37.613 --> 52:38.739
What?

52:40.324 --> 52:41.950
Is he a little kid or what?

52:44.203 --> 52:46.497
He just copies all sorts of stuff.

52:47.122 --> 52:49.583
I LOVE YOU, YOON SE-RI

52:49.666 --> 52:53.462
I LOVE YOU, YOON SE-RI

53:07.017 --> 53:08.352
Good morning.

53:09.019 --> 53:11.313
Don't go to work on an empty stomach.

53:11.397 --> 53:13.482
Make sure to eat at least an apple.

53:27.746 --> 53:29.581
Just so you know,

53:30.082 --> 53:33.168
it's good that you stick to your lane,

53:33.252 --> 53:36.630
but you shouldn't look only forwards.
You should look aside from time to time.

54:00.529 --> 54:02.281
Eat regularly at scheduled times.

54:02.906 --> 54:06.869
And don't eat alone.
Enjoy your meals with other people.

54:07.411 --> 54:08.495
With relish.

54:11.206 --> 54:14.418
So did you check the meat
as soon as you got here?

54:14.710 --> 54:17.337
Did you see that
at the entrance to the town?

54:17.588 --> 54:20.090
The way women looked at me...

54:20.174 --> 54:21.175
I didn't see it.

54:23.969 --> 54:27.055
Why don't you take a walk
for 30 minutes from 12:30 p.m.?

54:28.182 --> 54:30.767
I'll make sure
to go for a walk at that hour.

54:38.692 --> 54:40.319
It's good to have a walk.

54:40.903 --> 54:42.237
Jeong Hyeok.

54:43.280 --> 54:44.698
It's good to have a walk.

54:47.534 --> 54:48.577
Se-ri.

54:56.835 --> 54:58.003
Potato is good...

55:00.255 --> 55:01.673
as FF.

55:02.424 --> 55:03.509
What?

55:04.259 --> 55:07.429
Do you not know FF? The fried potato.

55:07.513 --> 55:09.556
What was the name again?

55:09.640 --> 55:11.934
-You mean French fries?
-Exactly.

55:12.017 --> 55:15.687
It's totally COMI.

55:15.771 --> 55:18.357
What does that mean?

55:18.440 --> 55:21.109
Do you not know what COMI means?

55:21.485 --> 55:25.364
It's crispy on the outside
and moist on the inside.

55:28.116 --> 55:29.993
It's no big deal.

55:30.744 --> 55:33.705
You just sound like a Seoul citizen.

55:35.582 --> 55:36.833
It actually suits me well.

55:39.086 --> 55:42.214
Actually, I turned on the faucet
and waited to get

55:42.297 --> 55:44.883
hot water this morning.

55:45.467 --> 55:47.302
So I was kind of surprised.

55:47.386 --> 55:50.472
I also waited
to get electricity for a while.

55:50.556 --> 55:51.723
I know.

55:52.182 --> 55:54.518
There has always been no electricity here.

55:54.601 --> 55:57.187
I can put up with all that.

55:58.272 --> 56:01.650
But it's frustrating
that there's no Internet connection here.

56:02.317 --> 56:04.820
It's feels like new hell.

56:05.404 --> 56:06.822
When I lie down at night,

56:07.447 --> 56:11.159
I see the video game screens
on the ceiling.

56:27.759 --> 56:30.679
Gosh, look who's here.

56:30.762 --> 56:32.347
Hello, Mrs. Go.

56:32.431 --> 56:34.683
It's been a long time.

56:34.766 --> 56:36.560
What brings you here?

56:36.643 --> 56:41.773
Dan is moving out
of her matrimonial home today.

56:43.442 --> 56:46.445
No, it's okay. Don't be like that.

56:46.528 --> 56:50.198
I feel so good and lighthearted.

56:50.282 --> 56:52.451
It's chilly out here.

56:52.534 --> 56:53.744
Why don't we go inside?

56:53.827 --> 56:55.245
Shall we?

56:55.329 --> 56:59.124
I recently went to Europe.

56:59.708 --> 57:01.209
-Europe?
-My gosh.

57:01.293 --> 57:02.878
I see.

57:02.961 --> 57:06.006
And I found some

57:06.089 --> 57:09.885
limited-edition products
you'd love a lot there,

57:09.968 --> 57:11.970
so I bought them.

57:12.095 --> 57:13.096
You bought them?

57:18.560 --> 57:19.561
Yeong, Wol?

57:20.562 --> 57:21.897
Myeong, Ok?

57:23.398 --> 57:25.901
I think it looks

57:25.984 --> 57:28.445
like me somehow.

57:28.528 --> 57:31.531
And this is how I looked
when I got married.

57:31.907 --> 57:33.742
This is no better than my actual face,

57:34.326 --> 57:36.495
but I'm sure it is me.

57:36.578 --> 57:37.996
-I looks the same.
-I know.

57:38.080 --> 57:41.625
-What is going on?
-My gosh.

57:41.708 --> 57:44.002
They are the new products

57:44.586 --> 57:47.047
from Se-ri's Choice for this spring.

57:47.798 --> 57:49.841
-Se-ri's Choice?
-Are you serious?

57:49.925 --> 57:52.344
Does it mean Se-ri did this for us...

57:52.427 --> 57:53.679
I know.

57:54.680 --> 57:55.847
My gosh.

57:55.931 --> 57:59.601
I said you don't have to
be like this around me.

57:59.685 --> 58:02.896
I don't have any grudge against the lady

58:02.980 --> 58:04.022
from down South.

58:04.106 --> 58:06.233
I can't kill my enemy

58:06.316 --> 58:08.527
when she doesn't come
under my observation.

58:08.610 --> 58:11.363
I can't even see her now.

58:11.446 --> 58:13.115
So I have no grudge.

58:14.366 --> 58:17.035
She wasn't here for a long time,
but she didn't forget us

58:17.661 --> 58:19.705
and made things like this for you guys.

58:20.580 --> 58:23.208
I don't think she's an ill-mannered lady.

58:23.291 --> 58:24.501
I know.

58:24.584 --> 58:25.919
She's not ill-mannered.

58:26.003 --> 58:28.171
She's really good at heart.

58:28.255 --> 58:31.383
The name of the limited line products

58:31.466 --> 58:33.677
of Se-ri's Choice for this season

58:34.928 --> 58:37.889
is saudade.

58:38.890 --> 58:39.933
It says saudade here.

58:40.017 --> 58:41.184
SAUDADE

58:41.768 --> 58:42.978
What do we do?

58:43.061 --> 58:44.312
What should we do?

58:44.396 --> 58:47.065
Gosh, I can't believe this.

58:49.609 --> 58:51.486
YEONG

58:51.570 --> 58:53.405
Does it say Yeong?

58:53.488 --> 58:54.531
Yes.

58:55.198 --> 58:57.159
And this is Wol as in Wol Suk.

58:57.868 --> 58:59.286
It says Myeong as in Myeong Sun.

58:59.369 --> 59:01.580
And this is Ok as in Ok Geum.

59:04.249 --> 59:05.876
So she got there safely.

59:06.752 --> 59:08.670
I guess she's doing fine.

59:09.421 --> 59:12.507
Apparently, she didn't forget us.

59:13.717 --> 59:15.260
I wish

59:16.219 --> 59:17.471
I could tell her

59:17.763 --> 59:19.681
that we got these

59:20.057 --> 59:22.309
and we will use them well.

59:22.517 --> 59:24.061
Where should I say that to?

59:24.978 --> 59:27.189
I believe she will know how we feel.

59:27.856 --> 59:29.149
I hope so.

59:35.906 --> 59:37.657
Do you see something over there?

59:37.741 --> 59:38.909
No.

59:40.869 --> 59:43.038
I'm tearing up because of the light
from the sky.

01:00:06.353 --> 01:00:07.979
What are you looking at?

01:00:08.647 --> 01:00:09.648
Aren't you coming down?

01:00:09.731 --> 01:00:11.691
No. I'll be right there.

01:00:11.775 --> 01:00:14.277
Give me ten minutes.
No, only five minutes.

01:00:14.361 --> 01:00:15.278
You have three minutes.

01:00:17.739 --> 01:00:19.157
What should I wear?

01:00:26.873 --> 01:00:28.834
Three minutes were too short.

01:00:29.501 --> 01:00:31.002
Do you like my clothes?

01:00:31.086 --> 01:00:32.963
I tried to look good.

01:00:35.006 --> 01:00:36.049
Well...

01:00:37.467 --> 01:00:40.345
I mean, this is our first date.

01:00:41.346 --> 01:00:42.514
It's not a date.

01:00:43.098 --> 01:00:44.808
The weather is so nice.

01:00:47.060 --> 01:00:49.062
-It's not so good.
-I like it, though.

01:00:52.357 --> 01:00:55.277
How does this place look
when flowers blossom?

01:00:55.694 --> 01:00:56.653
Well...

01:00:56.903 --> 01:00:58.071
I guess it's not bad.

01:00:58.155 --> 01:00:59.406
I see.

01:01:00.240 --> 01:01:04.077
I should come back here with you
when flowers blossom.

01:01:05.954 --> 01:01:07.330
I didn't say I'd do that.

01:01:07.914 --> 01:01:11.251
I'll be happy if you do.

01:01:16.756 --> 01:01:20.302
As spring wind blows

01:01:20.385 --> 01:01:24.514
Scattering cherry blossom petals

01:02:08.308 --> 01:02:09.559
First of all,

01:02:10.227 --> 01:02:11.311
you're pretty.

01:02:12.312 --> 01:02:14.231
And you make me want to become

01:02:15.065 --> 01:02:16.816
a better man.

01:02:16.900 --> 01:02:20.195
You're so amazing
that you make me feel that way.

01:02:21.238 --> 01:02:23.031
You are an amazing woman.

01:03:05.073 --> 01:03:06.366
I was thinking

01:03:07.659 --> 01:03:10.537
we should get together sometime.

01:03:10.870 --> 01:03:13.373
Thank you for coming all the way.

01:03:13.456 --> 01:03:15.792
I don't know what to say.

01:03:16.626 --> 01:03:17.836
It's okay.

01:03:18.461 --> 01:03:22.132
I had to come because
I'm the one who has something to say.

01:03:29.055 --> 01:03:31.558
Why are you doing this?

01:03:32.934 --> 01:03:36.521
I'm going to tell you
something I feel sorry about.

01:03:36.980 --> 01:03:39.190
So I apologized in advance.

01:03:45.322 --> 01:03:50.076
I'm afraid my daughter is not meant
to be with your son.

01:03:52.787 --> 01:03:53.913
Is it

01:03:55.332 --> 01:03:58.168
because you heard something about us?

01:03:59.586 --> 01:04:03.048
We wouldn't need other reasons.

01:04:06.051 --> 01:04:07.260
Dan says

01:04:08.011 --> 01:04:11.890
she doesn't want to marry Jeong Hyeok.

01:04:12.474 --> 01:04:16.519
I feel bad for her for spending
the past ten years on him, but...

01:04:16.978 --> 01:04:18.188
I am

01:04:19.939 --> 01:04:22.317
heartily sorry for that.

01:04:22.400 --> 01:04:25.612
Please don't be.
You don't have to apologize.

01:04:25.820 --> 01:04:28.615
I'm the one who should apologize.

01:04:29.741 --> 01:04:33.370
Jeong Hyuk got transferred
without telling his fiancée.

01:04:34.120 --> 01:04:36.247
And his parents didn't say anything

01:04:36.331 --> 01:04:39.167
other than that the wedding is postponed.

01:04:40.710 --> 01:04:42.504
I was upset back then.

01:04:43.004 --> 01:04:45.256
I wanted you to apologize to me.

01:04:46.174 --> 01:04:48.927
But things are different now.

01:04:50.095 --> 01:04:52.097
I'm breaking off

01:04:52.931 --> 01:04:56.976
this engagement
because my daughter doesn't want it.

01:04:58.311 --> 01:05:00.355
I should apologize.

01:05:01.773 --> 01:05:04.150
We weren't being considerate.

01:05:05.735 --> 01:05:08.196
There were complicated circumstances,

01:05:08.822 --> 01:05:10.573
but we didn't have a chance to explain...

01:05:10.657 --> 01:05:14.994
I will explain our circumstances.

01:05:16.204 --> 01:05:17.497
Dan

01:05:18.081 --> 01:05:20.542
has someone she loves.

01:05:22.752 --> 01:05:25.422
And the guy loves Dan...

01:05:30.343 --> 01:05:31.970
even more

01:05:32.929 --> 01:05:34.222
than his own life.

01:05:38.852 --> 01:05:40.437
So I have no choice.

01:05:41.396 --> 01:05:43.189
We only live once.

01:05:43.731 --> 01:05:45.900
And they love each other
more than their lives.

01:05:46.317 --> 01:05:48.236
There's nothing I can do about it.

01:05:53.241 --> 01:05:54.701
You are right.

01:05:55.869 --> 01:05:57.120
I agree with you.

01:05:58.621 --> 01:05:59.873
Do you?

01:06:01.040 --> 01:06:02.083
Yes.

01:06:04.878 --> 01:06:06.254
Mrs. Go.

01:06:07.547 --> 01:06:09.048
I'm truly sorry.

01:06:09.716 --> 01:06:11.050
And thank you.

01:06:41.956 --> 01:06:45.168
I said I would come
to see you this weekend.

01:06:46.252 --> 01:06:47.295
Right.

01:06:47.712 --> 01:06:49.172
I know that.

01:06:49.756 --> 01:06:54.219
But I wanted to come here again.

01:06:54.886 --> 01:06:56.638
I once came to this house

01:06:57.764 --> 01:06:59.140
while you were gone.

01:07:00.558 --> 01:07:01.893
To my house?

01:07:09.984 --> 01:07:11.611
I know a man like me

01:07:12.278 --> 01:07:14.322
should not do this

01:07:16.115 --> 01:07:19.160
to a woman like you, Dan.

01:07:23.248 --> 01:07:24.249
Still,

01:07:25.875 --> 01:07:27.168
I wanted to give it to you.

01:07:47.814 --> 01:07:50.191
I came here with Seung-jun.

01:07:50.775 --> 01:07:51.943
I see.

01:07:53.319 --> 01:07:55.655
He helped me a lot.

01:07:56.614 --> 01:07:58.032
Where is he now?

01:07:58.116 --> 01:07:59.492
I couldn't reach him.

01:08:01.035 --> 01:08:02.495
He went far away.

01:08:04.038 --> 01:08:06.082
He will never come back.

01:08:08.251 --> 01:08:10.044
But why...

01:08:10.962 --> 01:08:12.088
I don't know.

01:08:13.798 --> 01:08:16.134
I don't know the reason.

01:08:17.051 --> 01:08:19.679
A lot of things happen in life.

01:08:20.263 --> 01:08:23.975
And we can't explain
why most of them happen.

01:08:25.018 --> 01:08:28.605
When I went to Switzerland to see you,

01:08:29.731 --> 01:08:33.943
I didn't know the reason back then.

01:08:34.944 --> 01:08:36.863
The reason you kept taking pictures

01:08:37.155 --> 01:08:38.740
of the scenery

01:08:39.574 --> 01:08:41.993
when I'd gone all the way there
to see you.

01:08:47.957 --> 01:08:49.250
Shall we get some coffee...

01:09:48.601 --> 01:09:51.187
But the night when I came to this house,

01:09:52.897 --> 01:09:55.483
I could finally understand why.

01:10:05.034 --> 01:10:06.160
That's...

01:10:07.078 --> 01:10:10.498
I was looking for a candle that night
and found this by accident.

01:10:11.165 --> 01:10:14.377
I hated seeing that camera
in Switzerland so much

01:10:14.794 --> 01:10:16.421
that I recognized it immediately.

01:10:17.171 --> 01:10:19.924
I took it with me
so that I could throw it away.

01:10:20.717 --> 01:10:23.469
After all, I had been your fiancée
for the past ten years.

01:10:23.928 --> 01:10:26.055
I thought I had the right to do so.

01:10:30.977 --> 01:10:33.354
This is very old, so I'm sure it's broken.

01:10:33.438 --> 01:10:35.314
I got it fixed.

01:10:35.982 --> 01:10:38.317
And I finally found it.

01:10:39.318 --> 01:10:40.361
Found what?

01:10:43.656 --> 01:10:45.074
The reason...

01:10:46.826 --> 01:10:48.995
you refused to look at me
back in Switzerland.

01:10:55.501 --> 01:10:56.669
I guess

01:10:57.628 --> 01:10:59.881
this was meant to be.

01:12:06.739 --> 01:12:09.617
Don't live too happily, though.

01:12:48.739 --> 01:12:50.700
Today is the Mangzhong season.

01:12:51.117 --> 01:12:52.451
It's the day we plant seeds.

01:12:53.160 --> 01:12:55.329
What? Mangzhong?

01:12:55.955 --> 01:12:58.124
Was he a farmer in his past life?

01:12:58.958 --> 01:13:02.003
Gosh, Jeong Hyeok.

01:13:05.464 --> 01:13:06.841
So you'll be getting

01:13:07.300 --> 01:13:09.552
a flower pot.

01:13:12.179 --> 01:13:14.390
-What is this?
-You'll know what it is

01:13:14.765 --> 01:13:16.434
after you grow it.

01:13:17.101 --> 01:13:19.353
It may be sensitive and fussy,

01:13:19.437 --> 01:13:21.439
but if you do as you're told,

01:13:21.772 --> 01:13:24.901
it'll sprout after two weeks.

01:13:26.986 --> 01:13:28.821
You need to water it.

01:13:29.530 --> 01:13:32.366
But since it's sensitive to humidity,
don't give it too much water.

01:13:32.450 --> 01:13:34.994
-Give it moderate amount of water.
-How much

01:13:35.953 --> 01:13:37.163
is "moderate"?

01:13:39.749 --> 01:13:40.791
Is this enough?

01:13:41.792 --> 01:13:43.502
It needs sunlight as well.

01:13:44.128 --> 01:13:46.505
But don't put it under the sun
for too long.

01:13:46.589 --> 01:13:48.841
Keep it under the sun
for a moderate amount of time.

01:13:54.555 --> 01:13:58.684
And lastly, this is the most
important part when growing plants.

01:13:59.685 --> 01:14:01.938
You probably know well.

01:14:03.105 --> 01:14:05.066
Say ten nice things to it every day.

01:14:07.276 --> 01:14:09.278
This is so much work.

01:14:14.700 --> 01:14:17.286
Ms. Sold Out, upper price limit,
stock option,

01:14:17.370 --> 01:14:20.623
legendary sales, excellent brand,
high return,

01:14:20.706 --> 01:14:23.960
going public on the KOSDAQ,
the best in the field, limited-edition,

01:14:26.253 --> 01:14:27.296
and Ri Jeong Hyeok.

01:14:36.555 --> 01:14:37.640
What?

01:15:11.632 --> 01:15:13.050
How's Chairwoman Yoon doing?

01:15:13.968 --> 01:15:15.302
She's a bit strange.

01:15:15.511 --> 01:15:17.513
She's strange in a different way
this time.

01:15:18.180 --> 01:15:19.473
What is it now?

01:15:22.435 --> 01:15:23.811
She's a bit...

01:15:30.109 --> 01:15:31.402
excited.

01:15:37.575 --> 01:15:38.909
In between working,

01:15:38.993 --> 01:15:41.162
make sure to stretch and exercise.

01:15:43.330 --> 01:15:47.043
Let's talk about that
after the business trip next week.

01:15:47.126 --> 01:15:48.419
-Yes, ma'am.
-Yes, ma'am.

01:15:48.502 --> 01:15:50.921
As you all know, we've collaborated

01:15:51.005 --> 01:15:54.508
with a famous e-commerce company in China
for our upcoming products.

01:15:54.592 --> 01:15:57.595
We've incorporated
the new design patterns.

01:15:58.179 --> 01:16:00.347
This is from the first batch of samples.

01:16:00.431 --> 01:16:02.516
We'll be modifying them

01:16:02.600 --> 01:16:04.310
according to what you say,

01:16:04.393 --> 01:16:06.020
so please share your opinions with us.

01:16:06.103 --> 01:16:07.438
-Yes, ma'am.
-Yes, ma'am.

01:16:07.521 --> 01:16:11.067
She'd get upset at the slightest noise
when having a meeting.

01:16:11.317 --> 01:16:13.694
She was the most sensitive person ever.
However...

01:16:20.701 --> 01:16:21.952
I'm sorry.

01:16:25.664 --> 01:16:26.791
That's Chopin.

01:16:28.209 --> 01:16:30.169
I like his music too.

01:16:31.087 --> 01:16:33.756
My favorite one is "Nocturne."

01:16:36.050 --> 01:16:37.134
You should take that call.

01:16:37.218 --> 01:16:39.553
Thanks to her,
the rest of us can take a break as well.

01:16:40.137 --> 01:16:43.182
-Right. Let's go.
-Yes, ma'am.

01:16:50.189 --> 01:16:52.233
I like Chopin.

01:16:52.316 --> 01:16:54.360
I especially like "Nocturne."

01:16:54.652 --> 01:16:56.362
Seasons changed,

01:16:56.904 --> 01:16:59.031
but his messages kept coming.

01:17:00.616 --> 01:17:02.159
Today is Malbok.

01:17:03.911 --> 01:17:06.038
Thanks to you, I'll become

01:17:06.539 --> 01:17:08.332
a lunar calendar expert.

01:17:08.541 --> 01:17:10.918
Appreciate the flowers that bloom
during each season.

01:17:11.168 --> 01:17:13.921
Eat the dishes that are best
during each season.

01:17:19.885 --> 01:17:21.971
All right. It's Malbok today,

01:17:22.054 --> 01:17:23.722
so enjoy the chicken

01:17:23.806 --> 01:17:25.349
and go home early.

01:17:27.268 --> 01:17:30.521
I hope you won't miss the small happiness

01:17:31.438 --> 01:17:34.316
that you can and must find
in your everyday life.

01:17:35.276 --> 01:17:37.486
We've never welcomed spring

01:17:37.945 --> 01:17:41.407
or sweated during the summertime together.

01:17:41.824 --> 01:17:43.075
But thanks to his messages

01:17:43.659 --> 01:17:46.328
that came like presents
every few days or so,

01:17:46.871 --> 01:17:50.791
it felt like we were spending
every season together.

01:17:51.792 --> 01:17:55.045
I was afraid he'd feel sad if I were.

01:17:55.713 --> 01:17:59.383
So I tried my best to laugh, be thankful,

01:17:59.800 --> 01:18:02.553
and be happy.

01:18:18.652 --> 01:18:22.406
Since it's 12 a.m.,
it must be your birthday.

01:18:22.990 --> 01:18:24.283
Happy birthday.

01:18:25.576 --> 01:18:26.785
Thank you.

01:18:27.578 --> 01:18:30.372
I'm afraid this will be my last message.

01:18:31.123 --> 01:18:33.834
Apparently, reserved messages
have a one-year limit.

01:18:34.210 --> 01:18:36.962
And I must go now.

01:18:38.339 --> 01:18:39.506
Really?

01:18:40.090 --> 01:18:42.343
I wonder if the flowers have bloomed.

01:18:46.805 --> 01:18:47.806
They have.

01:18:48.641 --> 01:18:50.100
They're edelweiss.

01:18:53.229 --> 01:18:54.521
I know.

01:18:55.773 --> 01:18:59.610
Let's meet in the country
where those flowers bloom.

01:19:00.861 --> 01:19:02.988
I cannot tell you the exact date.

01:19:04.490 --> 01:19:05.449
But

01:19:06.617 --> 01:19:08.160
if we both

01:19:08.661 --> 01:19:09.912
try our best,

01:19:10.621 --> 01:19:13.165
perhaps, fate will be on our side.

01:19:13.791 --> 01:19:15.417
What is this?

01:19:16.627 --> 01:19:18.504
He's so vague.

01:19:24.510 --> 01:19:25.886
Hello, Yeong Ae.

01:19:25.970 --> 01:19:29.223
-They're warm.
-Hello, there.

01:19:29.306 --> 01:19:31.100
-Buy some tofu.
-Could you give me one?

01:19:31.183 --> 01:19:33.060
Sure. Here.

01:19:33.143 --> 01:19:34.144
Let's go.

01:19:34.228 --> 01:19:36.021
-How far have you gone?
-How far have you gone?

01:19:36.105 --> 01:19:37.982
-I'm at the village.
-I'm at the village.

01:19:38.065 --> 01:19:40.025
-How far have you gone?
-Here you go.

01:19:40.109 --> 01:19:41.235
I'd like one too.

01:19:41.318 --> 01:19:43.862
-Okay. Here you go.
-Thank you.

01:19:43.946 --> 01:19:45.155
-Enjoy.
-Thank you.

01:19:45.239 --> 01:19:46.365
I hope business will thrive.

01:19:46.448 --> 01:19:47.616
Goodbye.

01:19:52.329 --> 01:19:54.999
Right, is it today?

01:19:55.165 --> 01:19:56.875
Yes, it is.

01:19:58.335 --> 01:20:00.379
I can't believe it's been two months.

01:20:00.462 --> 01:20:03.841
I feel this way every time,
but it's been ages.

01:20:03.924 --> 01:20:06.010
I agree.

01:20:06.093 --> 01:20:09.471
Every time I feel Jeong Hyeok's absence
in this village,

01:20:09.555 --> 01:20:11.515
I have a great urge

01:20:11.598 --> 01:20:13.934
to send my husband,
who's doing nothing at home,

01:20:14.018 --> 01:20:15.769
to the outpost instead.

01:20:15.853 --> 01:20:18.605
You read my mind.

01:20:19.481 --> 01:20:21.567
All right, then. Shall we boil the eggs?

01:20:21.650 --> 01:20:23.360
Of course.

01:20:23.444 --> 01:20:25.654
I'll cook the dishes myself.

01:20:26.405 --> 01:20:28.699
And I'll fill his crocks like always.

01:20:29.283 --> 01:20:32.828
Great. Let's get to work
and meet in the afternoon.

01:20:51.305 --> 01:20:52.681
Aren't you cold?

01:20:52.765 --> 01:20:54.350
No, I'm not.

01:20:54.433 --> 01:20:55.893
I guess you didn't know.

01:20:55.976 --> 01:20:58.604
I naturally have a lot of heat in my body,

01:20:58.687 --> 01:21:00.939
so I don't feel cold at all.

01:21:01.774 --> 01:21:03.609
Hey, guys.

01:21:05.319 --> 01:21:06.487
What is it?

01:21:06.570 --> 01:21:08.489
Are your lips on fire?

01:21:08.572 --> 01:21:10.199
Oh, this?

01:21:10.366 --> 01:21:12.743
I paid a hefty sum to buy this
from the market.

01:21:12.826 --> 01:21:15.579
It's from the South.

01:21:16.080 --> 01:21:18.832
The name of this product is
"Lips that Bring about Spring."

01:21:19.166 --> 01:21:20.542
I beg to differ.

01:21:20.834 --> 01:21:23.545
I bet the anchovies will think
that it's chojang and charge at you.

01:21:23.629 --> 01:21:25.297
What did you just say?

01:21:25.881 --> 01:21:29.051
If you're all here,
why aren't you working?

01:21:29.134 --> 01:21:31.178
My, spin around.

01:21:33.972 --> 01:21:36.433
-Goodness, Yeong Ae!
-You look pretty.

01:21:37.643 --> 01:21:40.270
I'm just happy because spring is coming.

01:21:40.354 --> 01:21:41.438
Wow.

01:21:41.522 --> 01:21:44.858
Besides, I naturally have a lot of heat
in my body.

01:21:44.942 --> 01:21:47.236
-I see.
-I see.

01:21:52.616 --> 01:21:55.285
It's the spring breeze. Let's go inside.

01:21:55.369 --> 01:21:56.620
-Shall we?
-But I thought you had

01:21:56.703 --> 01:21:58.580
-It's the spring breeze.
-a lot of heat.

01:22:00.582 --> 01:22:03.585
It really feels nice to be here together.

01:22:03.669 --> 01:22:08.132
As the head of this village,
I should've done this earlier.

01:22:08.215 --> 01:22:11.009
I promise to do this more often
in the future.

01:22:11.093 --> 01:22:11.927
Right.

01:22:12.010 --> 01:22:13.720
Thank you.

01:22:13.804 --> 01:22:17.015
I'd appreciate it if you showed that much
hospitality to the new captain as well.

01:22:17.099 --> 01:22:19.309
Of course, don't you worry...

01:22:20.477 --> 01:22:21.478
What?

01:22:22.312 --> 01:22:23.397
What did you say?

01:22:25.065 --> 01:22:26.900
I have been discharged by my superiors

01:22:26.984 --> 01:22:30.070
and chosen as the pianist
for the National Symphony Orchestra.

01:22:30.154 --> 01:22:32.281
-Gosh, my blood pressure...
-Oh, dear.

01:22:32.364 --> 01:22:35.367
-What's wrong with me?
-Out of the blue?

01:22:35.617 --> 01:22:38.912
-Yes.
-This is too sudden.

01:22:38.996 --> 01:22:41.373
We're going to miss you terribly.

01:22:42.416 --> 01:22:44.501
The new captain will be living here,

01:22:44.585 --> 01:22:46.253
so please help him out.

01:22:47.171 --> 01:22:48.172
Goodness.

01:22:48.464 --> 01:22:50.716
Then

01:22:50.799 --> 01:22:53.385
who's the new captain?

01:22:58.849 --> 01:23:01.727
-I see.
-It's him.

01:23:02.060 --> 01:23:04.521
No, it's not him.

01:23:05.105 --> 01:23:07.274
It's him. Over there.

01:23:08.984 --> 01:23:10.360
What?

01:23:10.944 --> 01:23:12.321
-I see.
-I see.

01:23:15.365 --> 01:23:16.783
Are you talking about him?

01:23:17.242 --> 01:23:18.410
Yes.

01:23:19.745 --> 01:23:20.871
Hello.

01:23:20.954 --> 01:23:23.081
My name is Pyo Chi Su.

01:23:23.749 --> 01:23:26.001
I heard the villagers are so generous

01:23:26.084 --> 01:23:29.963
that the crocks are always filled
with meat.

01:23:30.255 --> 01:23:32.424
I do look forward to living here.

01:23:35.594 --> 01:23:38.764
That's actually a false rumor.

01:23:38.847 --> 01:23:42.809
And our villagers
aren't that generous either.

01:23:43.393 --> 01:23:46.146
To be honest, we're quite stingy.

01:23:46.230 --> 01:23:47.272
You're right.

01:23:47.356 --> 01:23:51.818
We're not the type to be
overly friendly with others.

01:23:51.902 --> 01:23:53.779
-We're not like that.
-No, we're not.

01:23:53.862 --> 01:23:56.657
You won't be able to help it.

01:23:57.533 --> 01:23:58.784
I see.

01:24:04.164 --> 01:24:05.999
If you leave like this,

01:24:06.208 --> 01:24:08.460
when will we be able to meet again?

01:24:08.877 --> 01:24:10.462
I'm sure we'll meet once again.

01:24:10.546 --> 01:24:12.381
If I get to perform once again,

01:24:12.464 --> 01:24:14.841
I'll invite you all to Pyongyang.

01:24:28.730 --> 01:24:30.065
Let's eat.

01:24:30.649 --> 01:24:33.026
-Thank you for the meal.
-Thank you for the meal.

01:24:33.110 --> 01:24:34.778
Thank you for the meal.

01:24:34.861 --> 01:24:36.655
Thank you for the meal.

01:24:36.863 --> 01:24:38.240
Eat up. Here.

01:24:39.241 --> 01:24:40.701
Give us the meat dish.

01:24:40.784 --> 01:24:41.660
Here.

01:24:42.411 --> 01:24:44.162
Here you go.

01:24:47.249 --> 01:24:48.917
Put that here.

01:24:49.543 --> 01:24:50.836
Here.

01:24:51.503 --> 01:24:53.630
-Eat up.
-You too.

01:24:57.342 --> 01:24:59.219
-Right?
-Yes.

01:25:01.805 --> 01:25:03.807
I haven't seen my husband
for quite a while.

01:25:03.890 --> 01:25:05.559
Where the heck is he?

01:25:23.952 --> 01:25:24.953
Have some.

01:25:54.900 --> 01:25:57.235
Goodness, I can't believe it.

01:25:57.319 --> 01:25:58.945
-Hi, Mom.
-Hey, honey.

01:25:59.029 --> 01:26:00.113
-Hi.
-Hey.

01:26:00.989 --> 01:26:05.035
I'm sorry. I spent all day playing golf.

01:26:05.118 --> 01:26:07.287
You weren't just playing golf.

01:26:07.371 --> 01:26:09.331
It's all part of your business.

01:26:11.041 --> 01:26:11.917
You're the best.

01:26:13.877 --> 01:26:17.047
It's the best choice you've made
in your lifetime.

01:26:17.339 --> 01:26:18.590
What?

01:26:18.757 --> 01:26:20.133
Playing golf?

01:26:20.217 --> 01:26:21.259
No.

01:26:21.677 --> 01:26:24.471
Agreeing to leave the business
in the hands of a professional manager.

01:26:24.554 --> 01:26:27.057
Look at how great the company is doing.

01:26:27.140 --> 01:26:28.892
Are you being sarcastic?

01:26:29.101 --> 01:26:30.060
No way.

01:26:31.061 --> 01:26:33.146
Mom, you should tell her that

01:26:33.230 --> 01:26:35.023
a professional manager
may manage our company,

01:26:35.107 --> 01:26:37.025
but I'm taking care of many things.

01:26:37.609 --> 01:26:39.611
I have to look into everything,

01:26:39.695 --> 01:26:41.905
give orders, and confirm things.

01:26:41.988 --> 01:26:44.157
Without me, this company would crumble.
Do you know that?

01:26:44.908 --> 01:26:45.992
Really?

01:26:46.326 --> 01:26:47.661
Yes, I'm telling you.

01:26:50.956 --> 01:26:52.082
If that's the case,

01:26:52.833 --> 01:26:56.211
may I suggest something?

01:26:56.962 --> 01:27:00.716
It's the most ideal business
if we want to reform our company.

01:27:04.010 --> 01:27:05.762
Let me hear it first. Tell me.

01:27:06.430 --> 01:27:09.683
Never mind. You don't have
any power anyway.

01:27:09.766 --> 01:27:11.268
Forget about it.

01:27:11.768 --> 01:27:13.937
What are you talking about?

01:27:14.020 --> 01:27:17.524
Mom, say something. I guess you won't.

01:27:17.607 --> 01:27:21.069
Look at the shares we have.
We have quite a lot.

01:27:21.153 --> 01:27:22.738
On top of that, I'm the eldest son.

01:27:22.821 --> 01:27:25.115
So why don't I have any power?

01:27:25.699 --> 01:27:27.576
Come on, tell me.

01:27:27.993 --> 01:27:30.704
It's about establishing
a scholarship foundation.

01:27:31.663 --> 01:27:34.082
-What?
-It's a foundation that supports children

01:27:34.166 --> 01:27:37.669
from low-income families, whether they be
in Korea or abroad,

01:27:37.753 --> 01:27:41.381
and teaches classical music
if they're talented.

01:27:42.591 --> 01:27:45.385
Many companies do that nowadays.

01:27:46.052 --> 01:27:49.848
I think we could send them
to a prestigious music college

01:27:50.432 --> 01:27:53.310
in Switzerland
where all the musical geniuses gather.

01:27:54.019 --> 01:27:55.020
Never mind.

01:27:55.437 --> 01:27:57.939
Not everyone can do this.

01:27:58.648 --> 01:28:01.318
What do you mean? We should do it.

01:28:01.401 --> 01:28:03.028
Honey, do this.

01:28:03.737 --> 01:28:05.781
You'll be raising musical geniuses.

01:28:06.364 --> 01:28:07.449
How awesome is that?

01:28:07.532 --> 01:28:08.950
-Do you think so?
-Yes.

01:28:09.201 --> 01:28:11.578
Are you sure you can do it?

01:28:11.661 --> 01:28:14.164
Look at her sounding me out.

01:28:14.247 --> 01:28:17.584
Do you think I wouldn't be able to do it?
It's a cakewalk.

01:28:17.918 --> 01:28:20.796
Then I'll introduce you to a staff,
so get started.

01:28:20.879 --> 01:28:22.005
Fine.

01:28:22.964 --> 01:28:25.008
Do you want to go to the department store
with me?

01:28:25.091 --> 01:28:26.927
Okay. What do you want?

01:28:27.219 --> 01:28:28.178
Keep me updated.

01:28:28.261 --> 01:28:29.679
-Bye.
-Okay.

01:28:31.598 --> 01:28:35.268
You'll be supporting musical geniuses
from all around the world.

01:28:35.936 --> 01:28:38.146
Honey, you're so awesome.

01:28:39.105 --> 01:28:40.690
You truly are.

01:28:40.774 --> 01:28:42.651
And this awesome man is yours.

01:28:42.734 --> 01:28:45.153
-You're the best.
-You're so awesome.

01:28:45.821 --> 01:28:50.408
ONE YEAR LATER

01:29:51.219 --> 01:29:52.387
Did you not see him?

01:29:55.932 --> 01:29:57.767
It won't be easy.

01:29:57.851 --> 01:29:59.352
The reporters are posting articles

01:29:59.436 --> 01:30:01.938
about how Se-ri's Choice and Queens Group

01:30:02.022 --> 01:30:04.649
have joined hands
in raising musical geniuses

01:30:05.442 --> 01:30:08.945
and are holding performances
once a year in Switzerland.

01:30:09.988 --> 01:30:11.865
I'm reaching out to him

01:30:11.948 --> 01:30:14.159
by posting these articles online.

01:30:14.868 --> 01:30:17.621
But there's no guarantee
that he'll read them

01:30:18.705 --> 01:30:23.001
or show up in Switzerland.

01:30:24.878 --> 01:30:26.171
It breaks my heart

01:30:26.254 --> 01:30:28.298
to see you return
in disappointment every time.

01:30:31.301 --> 01:30:32.594
Waiting for him

01:30:33.261 --> 01:30:35.055
is my only way of hanging in.

01:30:42.646 --> 01:30:43.855
But Mom...

01:30:44.731 --> 01:30:45.690
He...

01:30:47.233 --> 01:30:49.027
found me every time.

01:30:50.236 --> 01:30:51.905
No matter where I was.

01:30:52.489 --> 01:30:53.490
He will

01:30:55.742 --> 01:30:57.285
find me again someday.

01:31:01.373 --> 01:31:02.374
You're right.

01:31:03.375 --> 01:31:05.543
I'm rooting for you.

01:31:09.714 --> 01:31:10.924
Should you be heading out?

01:31:11.299 --> 01:31:13.343
I thought you were going to see Se-hyeong.

01:31:13.551 --> 01:31:14.594
Right.

01:31:15.095 --> 01:31:16.513
Our attorney is coming too.

01:31:17.931 --> 01:31:21.768
He's filing for divorce
while being incarcerated.

01:31:21.851 --> 01:31:23.561
Even I haven't done that.

01:31:24.479 --> 01:31:25.689
He's giving me a headache.

01:31:25.772 --> 01:31:26.981
I should go now.

01:31:28.233 --> 01:31:29.818
-Bye.
-Bye.

01:31:44.124 --> 01:31:48.002
Edelweiss symbolizes precious memories.

01:31:50.463 --> 01:31:52.465
What should I do, Jeong Hyeok?

01:31:53.591 --> 01:31:57.387
It's impossible for me to cherish you
just as a memory.

01:31:59.097 --> 01:32:00.348
So even if

01:32:00.974 --> 01:32:02.726
we don't meet this year,

01:32:03.226 --> 01:32:04.436
Maybe next year.

01:32:04.936 --> 01:32:06.688
If that doesn't work too,

01:32:07.105 --> 01:32:08.398
I'll anticipate the year after.

01:32:09.691 --> 01:32:11.985
Until the day you find me,

01:32:12.068 --> 01:32:13.361
I'll be waiting

01:32:14.112 --> 01:32:15.321
and praying.

01:33:15.799 --> 01:33:17.675
That's the decision I've made.

01:33:19.803 --> 01:33:22.472
We only get to live one life.

01:33:23.264 --> 01:33:26.434
But I have decided to spend mine

01:33:27.685 --> 01:33:30.730
encountering the love of my life,

01:33:31.356 --> 01:33:32.982
letting him go,

01:33:34.275 --> 01:33:38.279
and waiting to meet once again.

01:33:42.200 --> 01:33:44.452
That's what I've decided to do.

01:33:45.537 --> 01:33:46.996
So if you feel the same way,

01:33:48.498 --> 01:33:50.124
come to me.

01:34:36.129 --> 01:34:37.922
I always do this.

01:34:39.173 --> 01:34:41.509
I do well until right before the landing.

01:34:45.013 --> 01:34:46.222
In life,

01:34:46.890 --> 01:34:48.683
it's always the end that matters the most.

01:34:51.060 --> 01:34:54.063
I don't think your landing was that bad.

01:34:54.772 --> 01:34:59.068
I mean, I did land successfully,
but the ropes are all entangled.

01:34:59.694 --> 01:35:02.780
-I think you fell on the right spot.
-Look at this.

01:35:07.118 --> 01:35:09.495
No, let me correct myself.
You didn't fall.

01:35:09.871 --> 01:35:11.372
You've descended.

01:35:25.929 --> 01:35:27.388
I've missed you.

01:35:53.581 --> 01:35:55.124
I knew it.

01:35:58.211 --> 01:35:59.712
I knew

01:36:00.630 --> 01:36:02.131
you'd be able...

01:36:04.217 --> 01:36:06.386
to find me.

01:36:09.931 --> 01:36:12.308
But I still can't believe

01:36:13.601 --> 01:36:15.353
you've come all the way here.

01:36:19.440 --> 01:36:21.484
It must've been difficult.

01:36:21.985 --> 01:36:24.153
It must've been dangerous.

01:36:25.196 --> 01:36:26.364
How?

01:36:27.740 --> 01:36:29.659
How did you come here?

01:36:32.662 --> 01:36:34.455
I got on the wrong train.

01:36:41.671 --> 01:36:43.965
And that very train brought me here.

01:36:45.133 --> 01:36:47.260
It brought me to the place
I've yearned to come

01:36:48.428 --> 01:36:50.263
every morning and night.

01:36:53.516 --> 01:36:54.809
It brought me to my destination.

01:38:18.017 --> 01:38:20.311
I heard you are very good at what you do

01:38:20.394 --> 01:38:23.106
but only accept phone calls

01:38:23.189 --> 01:38:25.274
instead of allowing your clients
to visit you.

01:38:25.358 --> 01:38:28.277
A few years ago, I was arrested
by the control officers

01:38:28.361 --> 01:38:30.196
and had to spend some time behind bars.

01:38:31.030 --> 01:38:32.073
Oh, dear.

01:38:32.156 --> 01:38:35.076
Goodness, it must've been tough.

01:38:35.159 --> 01:38:37.537
Don't get me started.

01:38:37.620 --> 01:38:40.206
It was so terrible

01:38:40.289 --> 01:38:43.042
that the spirit that had possessed me
left me.

01:38:45.044 --> 01:38:46.045
"Left"?

01:38:46.587 --> 01:38:49.048
Doesn't that mean
she's no longer spiritual?

01:38:49.132 --> 01:38:50.466
You're right.

01:38:50.550 --> 01:38:53.553
That's why I couldn't offer my services
for some time.

01:38:53.636 --> 01:38:58.933
But recently,
a virgin ghost has possessed me.

01:38:59.016 --> 01:39:01.644
That's why I have outstanding foresight
when it comes

01:39:01.727 --> 01:39:04.564
to dating, marriage,
divorce, and remarriage.

01:39:04.647 --> 01:39:07.066
That's great news!

01:39:07.150 --> 01:39:10.319
When do you think
my daughter will get married?

01:39:12.530 --> 01:39:14.031
Let me see.

01:39:28.087 --> 01:39:32.842
There's only one man
who's the love of her life.

01:39:32.925 --> 01:39:36.596
But three years ago, they parted ways.

01:39:37.180 --> 01:39:40.141
That means there'll be
no more men in her life.

01:39:40.725 --> 01:39:42.435
She's pretty good.

01:39:42.518 --> 01:39:43.811
Shut up!

01:39:43.895 --> 01:39:47.231
However, she'll become
extremely successful.

01:39:47.315 --> 01:39:49.066
She'll go abroad quite often as well.

01:39:49.150 --> 01:39:52.653
With the amount of success she'll have,
she won't need a man.

01:39:52.737 --> 01:39:55.615
But still,

01:39:55.698 --> 01:39:58.117
she's going to be lonely.

01:39:58.201 --> 01:40:00.453
Could there be a solution to that?

01:40:03.748 --> 01:40:06.000
The solution lies within the capital.

01:40:06.584 --> 01:40:08.419
She could find a man in one year,

01:40:08.502 --> 01:40:10.213
six months,

01:40:10.296 --> 01:40:12.506
or even a month.

01:40:13.174 --> 01:40:14.967
Which one do you prefer?

01:40:15.051 --> 01:40:16.260
Pay her!

01:40:20.264 --> 01:40:21.432
What are you doing?

01:40:23.226 --> 01:40:26.812
I heard this fortuneteller was good.

01:40:27.188 --> 01:40:29.357
I was wondering when you'd get married.

01:40:29.941 --> 01:40:33.069
Didn't you always tell me
to live a trendy lifestyle?

01:40:33.486 --> 01:40:36.530
Then let's live that way.

01:40:36.989 --> 01:40:40.117
Being single is the trend nowadays.

01:40:40.201 --> 01:40:43.287
Well, you are right about that, but...

01:40:43.955 --> 01:40:46.916
I'll be busy preparing for my performance
in Russia next month.

01:40:47.166 --> 01:40:48.501
I'm going to rehearsal.

01:40:48.876 --> 01:40:49.877
Okay.

01:40:53.297 --> 01:40:55.800
Goodness, I know she's my daughter,

01:40:55.883 --> 01:40:57.718
but she's just fabulous.

01:40:58.552 --> 01:40:59.845
Ma'am.

01:41:00.471 --> 01:41:04.642
I'd like you to write
a one-month talisman.

01:41:04.850 --> 01:41:08.354
Myeong Eun, let her be.
She doesn't want to get married.

01:41:08.437 --> 01:41:11.148
I never said it was for her.

01:41:11.732 --> 01:41:13.943
Since she's so adamant about it,

01:41:14.026 --> 01:41:17.238
I'll let her live a flourishing life.

01:41:18.864 --> 01:41:20.199
But I'd like a man myself.

01:41:22.201 --> 01:41:25.496
Give me the best one you have.

01:41:53.649 --> 01:41:57.403
It's great news that you'll be moving
to Pyongyang,

01:41:57.486 --> 01:41:59.280
but we'll miss you terribly.

01:42:00.781 --> 01:42:02.950
If you don't want to
be looked down on there,

01:42:03.034 --> 01:42:04.910
you must look sophisticated.

01:42:04.994 --> 01:42:07.079
Stop by my salon to get your hair done.

01:42:07.163 --> 01:42:09.540
I'll give you the Goodbye Hairstyle.

01:42:10.875 --> 01:42:12.209
Thank you.

01:42:12.877 --> 01:42:15.838
I guess that fortuneteller
wasn't that bad.

01:42:15.921 --> 01:42:17.631
In any case, they are going far away.

01:42:18.215 --> 01:42:21.719
It's great news that they're leaving
to live a better life.

01:42:22.303 --> 01:42:24.555
For the past 30 years, her husband
worked in the dark

01:42:24.638 --> 01:42:26.849
while eavesdropping on others.

01:42:26.932 --> 01:42:29.560
Now, he finally gets to work
under the sun.

01:42:30.603 --> 01:42:34.648
You're right.
It's all thanks to Jeong Hyeok.

01:42:34.732 --> 01:42:35.775
That's right.

01:42:35.983 --> 01:42:39.445
By the way, didn't you say
that he got a job

01:42:39.528 --> 01:42:42.865
at 4.25 Arts Film Studio?

01:42:42.948 --> 01:42:44.700
Yes, you're correct.

01:42:44.784 --> 01:42:48.329
Then, what exactly does he do there?

01:43:10.059 --> 01:43:12.728
Products from the South?
We sell no such things.

01:43:12.812 --> 01:43:15.648
Are you positive?

01:43:16.273 --> 01:43:18.943
I heard they bought them here.

01:43:19.026 --> 01:43:20.319
That's impossible.

01:43:22.530 --> 01:43:25.866
Shampoo, conditioner, and body wash.

01:43:25.950 --> 01:43:28.911
I can't bear to take showers without them.

01:43:28.994 --> 01:43:32.164
What? You look like you'd manage
without a bar of soap.

01:43:33.332 --> 01:43:35.376
Anyway, we don't have them here.

01:43:36.460 --> 01:43:38.921
Gosh. We're not control officers.

01:43:40.840 --> 01:43:43.092
-You're not?
-He may look like this,

01:43:44.176 --> 01:43:47.096
but he's our captain.

01:43:47.763 --> 01:43:48.764
Hey.

01:43:52.143 --> 01:43:55.187
This is the most popular one these days.

01:43:55.396 --> 01:43:57.106
It's a new kind of shampoo.

01:43:57.189 --> 01:43:58.274
It's from Se-ri's Choice.

01:43:58.357 --> 01:43:59.400
"Se-ri..."

01:44:02.570 --> 01:44:04.822
Is this really that popular?

01:44:04.905 --> 01:44:06.407
Of course.

01:44:06.657 --> 01:44:07.825
It's the number-one best.

01:44:09.201 --> 01:44:13.122
That wench must be making a ton of money.

01:44:13.205 --> 01:44:14.623
You're right.

01:44:17.042 --> 01:44:18.210
I miss her.

01:44:19.503 --> 01:44:20.629
I miss my sister.

01:44:21.714 --> 01:44:23.299
Sister, my foot.

01:44:25.009 --> 01:44:28.512
I wonder if Captain Ri
has departed already.

01:44:29.346 --> 01:44:30.931
When we talked last week,

01:44:31.015 --> 01:44:32.933
he said he was departing this weekend.

01:44:33.017 --> 01:44:34.810
He must have left already.

01:44:36.103 --> 01:44:37.563
And I'm sure Se-ri's there as well.

01:44:45.571 --> 01:44:48.908
As you can see, the customers

01:44:50.367 --> 01:44:51.535
love it.

01:44:55.414 --> 01:44:56.582
That's great.

01:44:56.707 --> 01:44:57.791
Good work, everyone.

01:44:59.502 --> 01:45:00.753
You can go home now.

01:45:01.253 --> 01:45:02.796
Right. I'm sure you all know

01:45:02.880 --> 01:45:05.007
that I'll be on a two-week vacation
starting tomorrow.

01:45:05.090 --> 01:45:06.759
If something urgent pops up,

01:45:09.261 --> 01:45:12.014
decide what to do among yourselves
and push forward with it.

01:45:12.097 --> 01:45:16.602
My phone will be turned off.
I don't want any of you to call me.

01:45:17.394 --> 01:45:19.188
Ma'am, are you going to Switzerland again?

01:45:19.271 --> 01:45:21.732
Did you hide treasure there or something?

01:45:21.815 --> 01:45:25.194
You're not Heidi,
so why do you keep going there?

01:45:25.277 --> 01:45:26.278
Goodbye.

01:45:27.988 --> 01:45:30.241
-It's a guy, right?
-It's lasting a while this time.

01:45:30.324 --> 01:45:31.325
I think he's a foreigner.

01:45:31.408 --> 01:45:32.910
It's a long-distance one, right?

01:45:32.993 --> 01:45:36.413
We may have to write up
an English press release.

01:48:21.203 --> 01:48:22.746
He just started.

01:48:24.540 --> 01:48:25.749
I know.

01:51:41.486 --> 01:51:43.488
Subtitle translation by Young-ju Kim
